{"id":"G2021","lemma":"ἐπιχειρέω","transliteration":"epicheireō","sayIt":"epicheireō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to attempt","meaning":"ἐπιχειρέω, -ῶ\n(χεῖρ), [in LXX for חָשַׁב, Exo.9:25; גָּמַל, 2Ch.20:11, al. ;]\n1. to pat one's hand to.\n2. to take in hand, attempt: with inf., Luk.1:1, Act.9:29 19:13.†\n(AS)","glosses":["have undertaken","tried","who tried"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"luk-1","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"have undertaken","kjv":"have taken in hand"}},{"chapterId":"act-9","v":29,"renderings":{"bsb":"they tried","kjv":"they went about"}},{"chapterId":"act-19","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"who tried","kjv":"took upon them"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Luke 1:1","note":"Since many have undertaken to set in order a narrative concerning those matters which have been fulfilled among us,","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 9:29","note":"preaching boldly in the name of the Lord Jesus. He spoke and disputed against the Hellenists, but they were seeking to kill him.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20210","lemma":"δεξιάζω","transliteration":"dexiazō","gloss":"to approve"},{"id":"G20211","lemma":"δέσις","transliteration":"desis","gloss":"joint"},{"id":"G20212","lemma":"δεσποτεύω","transliteration":"despoteuō","gloss":"to enjoy ownership of . ."},{"id":"G20213","lemma":"δευτερολογέω","transliteration":"deuterologeō","gloss":"to speak a second time"},{"id":"G20214","lemma":"δηλαϊστός","transliteration":"dēlaistos","gloss":"wretched"},{"id":"G20215","lemma":"δημαγωγέω","transliteration":"dēmagōgeō","gloss":"be popular"},{"id":"G20216","lemma":"διαβιάζομαι","transliteration":"diabiazomai","gloss":"penetrate"},{"id":"G20217","lemma":"διαγορεύω","transliteration":"diagoreuō","gloss":"to declare"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}